    "narrative": {
      "care_continuity": [
        "SitRep78 reports 760 patients in isolation (348 confirmed / 412 suspected) at 72.4% national occupancy; Ituri is 525/821 = 63.9%, while Nord-Kivu remains over capacity at 196/141 = 139.0%.",
        "National movement totals exclude Haut-Uele admissions and exits. Adding the observed Haut-Uele net change to the reported flow yields 761, one above the stated 760 end-of-day census; the source itself notes a one-patient Nord-Kivu mismatch.",
        "The SitRep reports 163 facilities preselected for free essential-care support, but only 43 already receive partner support; the no-fee directive and contracting remain incomplete.",
        "Only 181 of 1170 triage units are reported functional. Frontline burden is at least 155 confirmed infections and 44 deaths across Ituri, Nord-Kivu and Haut-Uele, with three Ituri infections not yet assigned to zones.",
        "Continuity of essential health services remains explicitly compromised, increasing indirect non-Ebola mortality."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "The official footprint remains 49 of 140 health zones across five provinces. Wanie-Rukula is described as a fifth Tshopo zone, but its seventh provincial case remains excluded pending harmonization.",
